  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 225 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nThursday night through Tuesday:\n\nHigh pressure will continue to build back into the region. No \nsignificant weather is expected with low temperatures in the upper \n50s inland and low 60s near the lakeshore. Winds will be light and \nfrom the southeast.\n\nBy Friday winds will shift to be from the southwest ahead of the \nnext weak surface front to move through the region. Hot and humid \nconditions return as high temperatures will peak around 80F and \ndewpoint temperatures will top in the mid 60s. Expect lows Friday \nnight to be around the low/mid 60s. As the front moves through \nFriday night, a stray shower or two may pop-up, but will be weak and \nshort lived (~15% chances).\n\nSaturday morning will see rain chances diminish, but this will not \nlast long as low pressure from the Great Plains moves eastwards.\nSeveral shortwaves will pass over the region starting Saturday night \nwhich along with the heat and humidity (heat index near 90F) will \nact as a starting point for showers and storms to return through the \nend of the weekend (~30-50% chances) and into the beginning of next \nweek (~40-70% chances). Timing and severity of these storms remain \nuncertain at this time, but will become clearer as the weekend nears.\n\nSoergel",
